{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-point","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:categorical-point","kind":"definition","title":"Categorical point","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-universe"],"tags":["point","categorical"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalPoint","text":"categorical-point.md","leanSource":"categorical-point.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"def:categorical-point\"></a>\n<strong>Definition.</strong> <em>Categorical point</em></p>\n<p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum universe. A <strong>categorical point</strong> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> is a morphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p \\colon \\mathbf{1} \\to A</code>. In the archimedean realisation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A = C^\\infty(M)</code>, a categorical point corresponds to evaluation at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p \\in M</code>. The augmentation ideal at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code> is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{m}_p = \\ker(p^* \\colon A \\to \\mathbf{1})</code>, and the germ of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code> is the quotient <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A / \\mathfrak{m}_p^2</code>.</p>\n"}
